# .pen Design File Naming Conventions

When creating or modifying nodes in `.pen` design files, follow these naming conventions strictly.

## Reusable Components (`reusable: true`)

**Pattern:** `{Category} / {Component} / {State}`

- Title Case, separated by ` / ` (space-slash-space)
- Category groups related components (e.g. `Chat`, `Nav`)
- State is required for interactive elements

Examples:
- `Chat / Send Button / Default`
- `Chat / Voice Button / Disabled`
- `Nav Item / Active`
- `Nav / Toggle Button Hover`

## Component Instances (`type: ref`)

**An instance MUST have the exact same name as the component it references.**

- Pencil visually distinguishes parent components (pink outline) from instances (purple outline), so there is no reason to rename instances.
- Using different names for the same component across instances creates confusion and defeats the purpose of a design system.

## Rules

1. **No unnamed refs.** Every `type: ref` node must have a `name`. No exceptions.
2. **Instance name = component name.** Instances use the exact same name as their parent component. Do not abbreviate, reformat, or add suffixes.
3. **One component, one name, everywhere.** If the component is `Chat / Send Button / Disabled`, every instance of it is also named `Chat / Send Button / Disabled`.
